CAPPED-TIER CDC STRESS — can a 0.5 CPU / 256 MB drain keep up with
1,000,000 changed rows per table per minute across 30 tables in one group?
raw log, generated 2026-10-04T09:01:13Z on the bench VPS
host: 16 cores, 61 GB RAM, shared with production

===== 1. the tool and its provenance, asserted from inside the cage
  apitap.__version__       0.57.0
  interpreter              3.13.3 (abi3 wheel)
  _apitap.abi3.so md5      41e9f7c252d3e1eb5403b70f87bf5435
  the site-packages is bind-mounted READ-ONLY at /py and put on PYTHONPATH, so
  the PyPI wheel is what runs and nothing is built on this box. Every leg
  re-asserts it from inside the cage — e.g. the stress drain's own log:
